data a_hand_cost_citation_contradicts_the_realization_it_prices: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_hand_cost_citation_contradicts_the_realization_it_prices" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the accumulator-copy lens prices a combiner from the std.primitive_identity PrimitiveCostFact of the declaration it routes through, read by declaration through primitive_modeled_cost_for_declaration with the realizing carrier selected, sufficient for list_snoc_item to be priced at the persistent reading and for a hand citation that disagrees with the declaration's modeled cost to have no route into a verdict" } },

  receipts: [
    "**A cost lens prices an operation from a hand-authored citation whose cost contradicts every realization that runs.** INVALID STATE: v2.lens.cost.copied_port_citations copied_port_citation_list_snoc_item cites std.algebra list_snoc_item (`xs |> list_push(item)`) as an Arrow whose Loop body is linear in xs. The accumulator-copy lens derives its copied port from that citation, so a per-item append fold is convicted as a copied accumulator. HARM: the verdict is directional and wrong. It convicts the linear construction and is cited as coverage, which is the false positive measured on v2.compiler.tokenize lexeme_grow (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode lens_prices_the_authority_while_the_lane_runs_the_realization). The citation is a second cost authority for one operation, and nothing joins it to the declaration's modeled cost (DESIGN section 3).",
    "EVIDENCE THAT THE CITATION IS WRONG, read from the realizations, not assumed (zesty-ibex-193, 2026-10-24). Both routes that run list_push use im 15.1.0 Vector. The emitted bridge v1_rt rc_list_push is Rc::make_mut, then push_back. The interpreter's method_call.list_push arm (v1_interpreter.rs) clones the RrbVector, then push_back. im 15.1.0 src/vector/mod.rs documents Vector clone as 'Time: O(1), or O(n) with a very small, bounded n for an inline vector' and push_back as 'O(1) amortised, and O(log n) in the worst case'. So no running realization is linear in xs. The modeled fact now says the same: std.primitive_identity primitive_list_push_cost, persistent reading log n worst case and amortized constant, read by declaration and executed in test.claim.primitive_modeled_cost_witness.",
    "WHY THE CITATION SURVIVED: it was authored as 'faithful' to an accumulator-copy axis (its semantics_note says so), not derived from the realization or from a cost contract. The only contract that stated list_push's cost, std.primitives list_push_contract, was never read by any lens, so the contradiction had no place to surface (gunbc.rung_drop.retired_contract_cost_facts_drop records that the contract's cost had no executing consumer).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder. The wrong verdict is produced silently, and nothing refuses it. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The lens can read the declaration's modeled cost, so a citation that disagrees with it has no route into a verdict. NEXT TRIGGER: climbable now but unbuilt. Correcting this citation is the first change of the lens-repoint PR that follows the declaration-keyed cost carrier (parent ruling sleek-owl-397, 2026-10-24), and it changes the lens's verdicts. It needs the realizing carrier selected, because the modeled fact holds one reading per carrier.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.cost.copied_port_citations", decl_name: "copied_port_citation_list_snoc_item", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.primitive_identity", decl_name: "primitive_list_push_cost", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "list_snoc_item", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
